{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2453","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2453","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2453\",\"parent_revision\":\"f3d74c6bebe84547b8974b98673f9b34e6bf569b32da645df402509e708f49e8\",\"root_revision\":\"f3d74c6bebe84547b8974b98673f9b34e6bf569b32da645df402509e708f49e8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring the #2437 grooming session, the groomer agent wrote sections under non-canonical names: \\\"RT-ICA Assessment\\\" instead of \\\"RT-ICA\\\", \\\"Artifact Classification\\\" instead of the canonical name. The output validation gate in finalize.md checks for exact section names. The name mismatch caused the gate to report the RT-ICA section absent even though content existed. The orchestrator had to write the section manually under the correct name to unblock the workflow.\\n\\nRoot cause: there is no single source of truth for section names that agents read before writing. Each agent invents or recalls section names from its own prompt context, creating divergence between what agents write and what the validation gate expects.\\n\\n**Two design directions to address this:**\\n\\n**Option A \u2014 backlog-sections.md reference document**\\n\\nCreate a file (e.g. plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-sections.md) that is a diagram or table showing: which agent or phase is responsible for generating each section, the exact canonical section name to use as input to backlog_groom, and which downstream agents or validation steps consume each section. Agents receive this file as a required prerequisite before writing any section. The agent's prompt includes a self-check checklist: for each section you wrote, verify the name you used matches the canonical name in backlog-sections.md exactly, character for character.\\n\\n**Option B \u2014 structured output contract per agent role**\\n\\nA more robust approach: define a state machine or queue that tracks what stage the grooming job is at. For each agent role (impact-analyst, fact-checker, rtica-assessor, classifier, groomer), the system surfaces: the exact input artifacts the agent needs and where to retrieve them, the exact output structure as a JSON schema including section titles and the MCP call signature (backlog_groom with section parameter), and links to additional resources. The agent receives this as its task brief rather than a free-form prompt. The MCP call is pre-validated against the JSON schema before the server accepts the write, rejecting non-canonical section names at the boundary.\\n\\nBoth options eliminate the current failure mode where an agent invents a section name that passes through backlog_groom but fails the downstream validation gate. Option B additionally prevents the problem at the write boundary rather than the read boundary.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claim 1**: The groomer output validation gate in `groomer-output-validation.md` uses exact string matches against section names returned by `backlog_view().sections`.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` lines 13-24 \u2014 Required Section Schema table lists section names as exact strings: `RT-ICA`, `Impact Radius`, `Fact-Check`, `Acceptance Criteria`, `Reproducibility`, `Issue Classification`, `Priority`, `Design Intent Alignment`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 2**: There is currently no single file or module that agents can read to discover the canonical section names before calling `backlog_groom`.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n\\nSOURCE: Read all 5 swarm agent files (`rtica-assessor.md`, `classifier.md`, `impact-analyst.md`, `alignment-analyst.md`, `backlog-item-groomer.md`) \u2014 none contains a reference to `rendering.py`, `SECTION_HEADING`, or `groomer-output-validation.md` as a pre-write lookup step. The canonical names exist in Python source code (`rendering.py:34-38`) and in the validation reference doc but are not wired to agent write steps.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 3**: The `backlog_groom` MCP tool's `section` parameter currently accepts any string \u2014 it does not reject non-canonical names at the write boundary.\\n\\n**Verdict**: VERIFIED\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:873-898` \u2014 `_normalize_section_key()` resolves known aliases but returns unknown names unchanged (`return name`). No error is raised for unrecognised section names. The function is called in the `backlog_groom` write path.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-05-28\\n**Decision**: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING\\n\\n| Condition | Status | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent \u2014 agents write wrong section names causing downstream validation failure | AVAILABLE | Item description cites #2437 session; `groomer-output-validation.md` confirms exact-string-match gate |\\n| Root cause \u2014 no shared source of truth for section names before agents write | AVAILABLE | Confirmed: `SECTION_HEADING` dict in `rendering.py:34-38` is the authoritative mapping but is not surfaced to agents |\\n| Canonical section names list | AVAILABLE | `rendering.py:34-38` defines `fact_check\u2192Fact-Check`, `rt_ica\u2192RT-ICA`, `issue_classification\u2192Issue Classification`; `groomer-output-validation.md` lists all 8 required sections with exact names |\\n| MCP write boundary behavior \u2014 does backlog_groom reject non-canonical names? | AVAILABLE | `operations.py:873-898` `_normalize_section_key()` normalises known aliases but does not reject unknown names \u2014 passes through unchanged |\\n| Validation gate location and logic | AVAILABLE | `groomer-output-validation.md` \u2014 `backlog_view().sections` exact-string-match check runs in Step 8.7 |\\n| Agent prompt surfaces for section names | AVAILABLE | All 5 swarm agent files read: rtica-assessor, classifier, impact-analyst, alignment-analyst, backlog-item-groomer \u2014 none reference `SECTION_HEADING` or `rendering.py` |\\n| Option A feasibility \u2014 reference doc pattern | AVAILABLE | Codebase already has reference docs consumed by agents (e.g. `groomer-output-validation.md`); pattern is established |\\n| Option B feasibility \u2014 MCP validation at write boundary | AVAILABLE | `_normalize_section_key()` in `operations.py` already has alias resolution; adding strict-mode rejection is a code change to one function |\\n| Downstream consumers of groomed sections | AVAILABLE | `groomer-output-validation.md` lists required sections and minimum content; plan-phase agents consume via `backlog_view(sections=[...])` |\\n\\nAll conditions AVAILABLE from codebase evidence. No MISSING conditions. APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-28)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 This is a recurring failure mode in every grooming swarm run. The Step 8.7 retry loop (haiku \u2192 haiku retry \u2192 sonnet \u2192 blocked) consumes significant agent budget when triggered by a name mismatch. The root cause (no shared source of truth) will continue to produce the same failure until addressed. P1 priority is appropriate.\\n\\n**Effort**: Small \u2014 The gap is a missing reference document and/or a one-function change to `_normalize_section_key()`. Option A requires: create one reference doc, add one line to each of 5 agent prompts. Option B requires: modify `_normalize_section_key()` to accept a strict mode flag, update `backlog_groom` parameter schema, add error message. Both are bounded changes with clear file targets.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A canonical section names reference is readable by agents before any `backlog_groom(section=...)` call \u2014 either as a prose reference doc or as a MCP tool response.\\n2. All 5 swarm agent files (rtica-assessor, classifier, impact-analyst, alignment-analyst, backlog-item-groomer) reference or load the canonical names source before writing their section.\\n3. Running a grooming swarm on any backlog item results in all required sections present under their exact canonical names as listed in `groomer-output-validation.md` without orchestrator intervention.\\n4. The Step 8.7 validation gate passes on the first attempt for items groomed after this change \u2014 no retry loop is triggered by section name mismatches.\\n5. If Option B is selected: `backlog_groom(section='RT-ICA Assessment')` returns a validation error naming the canonical section (`RT-ICA`) and refusing the write. `backlog_groom(section='RT-ICA')` succeeds.\\n6. The `SECTION_HEADING` dict in `rendering.py` remains the single authoritative source \u2014 the reference doc or schema is derived from it, not maintained independently.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|---|---|\\n| Source of truth \u2014 canonical names | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/rendering.py` \u2014 `SECTION_HEADING` dict lines 34-38 |\\n| Alias normalization | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 `SECTION_HEADING_ALIAS` lines 469-473 |\\n| Normalization logic | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `_normalize_section_key()` lines 873-898 |\\n| Validation gate spec | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` |\\n| Agent prompt templates | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` |\\n| Swarm agents | `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md`, `classifier.md`, `impact-analyst.md`, `alignment-analyst.md`, `backlog-item-groomer.md` |\\n| Skill orchestration | `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all required information is AVAILABLE in the codebase\\n- Blocks: Any grooming swarm run that triggers the Step 8.7 retry loop due to section name mismatch; backlog item #1774 (dispatch discipline inline) uses same reference-doc pattern and may benefit from parallel implementation\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n\\n**Rationale**: The development harness design principles state \\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact\\\" and the harness owns the process. Establishing a shared source of truth for section names reinforces the harness's ownership of process contracts \u2014 it prevents agent autonomy from degrading the validation gate. Both Option A (reference doc) and Option B (MCP write-boundary validation) are consistent with the harness design pattern: Option A extends the existing reference-doc pattern used by `groomer-output-validation.md`; Option B extends the existing alias-normalization in `_normalize_section_key()`. Neither option requires a new architectural layer.\\n\\nSOURCE: `plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 \\\"The harness owns the process; language plugins own the specialists\\\" and \\\"Every stage produces an MCP-registered artifact (stateless handoff)\\\".\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n\\n**Rationale**: The system behaved as designed \u2014 `backlog_groom` accepted the agent-supplied section name and wrote it. No code was broken. The failure occurred because a quality gate that should have caught the mismatch at write time does not exist. Agents are free to supply any string as `section=`, and the validation gate only fires after the full swarm completes (Step 8.7), by which point the wrong name is already persisted. The fix is adding the guardrail \u2014 either at the agent prompt level (reference doc) or at the MCP write boundary \u2014 not fixing broken code.\\n\\n**Analysis method**: none required \u2014 classification is directly observable from the failure mode description.\\n\\n**Scenario target**: grooming swarm, any of the 5 specialist agents (rtica-assessor, classifier, impact-analyst, alignment-analyst, backlog-item-groomer) writing a section via `backlog_groom(section=...)`.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A for feature items \u2014 this is a missing-guardrail classification. The failure mode is observable but not a bug in code:\\n\\n1. Spawn a grooming swarm for any backlog item\\n2. In any swarm agent prompt, do not provide the canonical section name\\n3. Agent writes section under an invented name (e.g. `RT-ICA Assessment` instead of `RT-ICA`)\\n4. Step 8.7 validation gate (`groomer-output-validation.md`) reports the section absent\\n5. Swarm retries up to 4 times before blocking\\n\\nReproducible from #2437 session context: orchestrator had to manually write the section under the correct name after the gate failed.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: grooming section names need a shared source of truth with exact output contracts per agent so agents can self-verify section names before writing** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] Code path: `operations.py` `_normalize_section_key()` \u2014 MCP write normalization\\n- [x] Data definition: `rendering.py` `SECTION_HEADING` + `models.py` `SECTION_HEADING_ALIAS`\\n- [x] Validation gate: `groomer-output-validation.md` Step 8.7\\n- [x] Agent prompts: 5 swarm agents, all writing sections without consulting canonical names\\n- [x] Prompt templates: `groomer-agent.md` \u2014 spawn prompts for groomer agent\\n- [x] Skill orchestration: `groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- [ ] Reference document for agents: does not exist \u2014 this is the gap\\n- [ ] MCP schema validation: `backlog_groom` accepts any string for `section` \u2014 no rejection gate\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 work-backlog-item #2437 grooming swarm 2026-05-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| System | Role | Impact |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/rendering.py` | Defines `SECTION_HEADING` dict \u2014 authoritative canonical names | Must be referenced or exported for agents to read |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` | Defines `SECTION_HEADING_ALIAS` \u2014 lowercased alias normalization | Source of truth for alias resolution logic |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` | `_normalize_section_key()` \u2014 MCP write path normalization | Option B would add rejection of unrecognised names here |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/rtica-assessor.md` | Writes `RT-ICA` section | Must receive or look up canonical name before calling `backlog_groom` |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/classifier.md` | Writes `Issue Classification` section | Must receive or look up canonical name |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/impact-analyst.md` | Writes `Impact Radius` section | Must receive or look up canonical name |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/alignment-analyst.md` | Writes `Design Intent Alignment` section | Must receive or look up canonical name |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/fact-checker.md` | Writes `Fact-Check` section | Must receive or look up canonical name |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` | Writes all remaining required sections | Must receive or look up canonical names |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-output-validation.md` | Validation gate that checks exact section names after swarm completes | Change in canonical names must be reflected here |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md` | Contains prompt templates for spawning groomer agents | Any new section-name pre-check step must appear here |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` | Orchestrates swarm steps | References `groomer-output-validation.md`; swarm spawn steps may need canonical name injection |\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"efd7a5ba9dde35e4f93f82c4a91d48adba0d82f0f86525d4959816d4ecb619f8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTAmyA\"}"}